From f49501d77e6b78ca7acf7f6807c4be8f603546ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:57:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] soc: apple: aop: Start every AFK endpoint the T6050
 firmware advertises

The K116s AOP firmware (27.2, AppleAOPAudioFirmware-610.18) advertises
AFK endpoints 0x20-0x27 and 0x29-0x30. Its boot stage "setup_endpoints"
brings them up one at a time and waits for the host's STARTEP on each
("waiting for endpoint enable, _routing=0x2f" in its log, where the value
is route << 16 | endpoint). The driver only knew 0x20-0x2e, so the
firmware waited for 0x2f (als-temp-2) forever, never reached its
system_ready and services_ready stages and announced no EPIC service: no
aop-audio, so no sound card, and no sensors.

Cover 0x2f and 0x30 (devmotion3). The firmware then announces its 20
services and the card registers.

aurora-silicon/linux #1645 (ported by Thomas Glanzmann, sithglan), commit
367e36d02939, merged upstream in 03f060b251c8; applied unchanged on a34d26c2.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
index 2452ae5035d7..95c9c8bcdea7 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@
 /// The DART page size the firmware segments are mapped with.
 const FW_REGION_PAGE: u64 = 0x4000;
 const AFK_ENDPOINT_START: u8 = 0x20;
-const AFK_ENDPOINT_COUNT: u8 = 0xf;
+const AFK_ENDPOINT_COUNT: u8 = 0x11;
 const AFK_OPC_GET_BUF: u64 = 0x89;
 const AFK_OPC_INIT: u64 = 0x80;
 const AFK_OPC_INIT_RX: u64 = 0x8b;
